Where all else along the great eastern cliffs seems to be sheer and impassable,
here where the jungle gives way to the incessant beating of the waves upon the 
shore there seems to appear a path, steep and treacherous, down to the jungle
below. You see the cliffs sink down to a white-sanded beach just below where 
you now stand. Rocks slip from the path and tumble down to the seashore many
seconds later, causing you to adhere more closely to the path downward.
